DOOMSDAY CLOCK MOVED AHEAD ON NEWS THAT FORMER SPICE GIRL JOINS TV SHOW
"FRIENDS"

The Bulletin of Concerned Scientists moved the Doomsday Clock ahead by
five minutes in reaction to the news that former Spice Girl Jeri
Haliwell will be joining the cast of the television show Friends.  "In
light of the recent surge in ratings for Jerry Springer, the Vanity Fair
photos of Monica Lewinsky and the continuing success of the group
Hanson, we felt this latest development brought us even closer to the
end of civilization," chairman Leonard Reiser said.  The clock was last
advanced last Fall after the release of the Kevin Costner movie "The
Postman" and the announcement by America Online that they had signed up
over 12 million members.

