"POPE SPICE" ON DECK?

VATICAN CITY (DPI) -- After a visibly ailing Pope visited Mexico and the
U.S. last week, many papal pundits are speculating about who will
succeed him.  Daily Probe sources way outside the Vatican have confirmed
that the front runner is none other than Geraldine Estelle Halliwell,
better known to some as the former Ginger Spice.  Flush from her
successful appointment as UN Ambassador of Pre-Pubescent Affairs, the
idea of her being the next Pope doesn't seem any so far-fetched any
more.  Certainly, nay-sayers are nitpicking that she's not Catholic
(Anglican), far from virginal, has appeared nude in Playboy, and is
rather "womanesque"; but that doesn't seem to be slowing the groundswell
forming for her future appointment.  When asked, an anonymous Vatican
insider said wistfully, "A hotty like that as the Pope would make me
consider giving up my subscription to 'Choir Boy Weekly'."  Pope John
Paul II himself commented, "Even though she left the group, people would
call her 'Pope Spice,' which sounds too much like 'Posh Spice,' and
would be all together too confusing.  I'm against it."

Reported by Diana K. Heche

